{
  "about": "Corner pin (row 73): each corner of a clip is pinned to a point in the clip's own box, (0, 0) its top left and (1, 1) its bottom right, before its rotation, so moving, scaling or turning the clip carries the pin; params `cornerPin.enabled` and `cornerPin.<topLeft|topRight|bottomRight|bottomLeft><X|Y>` in percent of the box (capped -500 to 600; the default corners, a bow tie, a dent or corners on one line mean no pin). `read` is the param reading (apps/web/src/corner-pin/pin.ts and crates/editor/src/corner_pin.rs); `homography` is the perspective map the shared compositor draws with (crates/compositor/src/corner_pin.rs): `forward` takes a texture point (uv) to the box, `inverse` a box point to uv (null beyond the horizon); `canvas` places the pinned corners on the canvas for handles. Expected values from an independent Python reference (exact 8x8 solve).",
